WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.875
The rest of the gaps are about what
a program needs around one policy.

2
00:00:03.875 --> 00:00:07.337
A field the stable API
marks required is missing.

3
00:00:07.337 --> 00:00:10.001
There's no JSON at all
for the risk policy.

4
00:00:10.001 --> 00:00:12.613
The results live only in the admin center,

5
00:00:12.613 --> 00:00:15.463
where a pipeline can't
keep them as evidence.

6
00:00:15.463 --> 00:00:18.950
There's no record of who's in
scope, who's out, and why.

7
00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:21.150
And there are no rings and no alert,

8
00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:25.237
so enforcement is all or nothing
and nobody hears about a block.

9
00:00:25.237 --> 00:00:29.690
So the verdict: keep the sample's shape,
and don't create it as published.
